aired CIs, and the list of graph families with held-out counts.\n- **Length:** the venue requires 8–9 body pages. The task brief allows a short paper but sets no maximum, so I followed the venue.\n- **Supplement:** full per-family table, evaluation protocol and validity checks, seeds and reproduction details, the selection-scope disclosure, and the required LLM Usage section.\n\n**Things the writer must handle:**\n- **Seed range of 0:** all three evaluation runs gave identical errors because the model is deterministic and the labels are fixed. This says nothing about robustness; the bootstrap is the only source of uncertainty.\n- **Feature collisions:** 12 held-out graphs share their exact six-statistic vector with another graph, so any statistics-only predictor must give them the same prediction.\n- **Matthews reference (0.605):** it needs the full graph, not cheap statistics, and has no paired CI, so it should not be described with significance language.\n- **References:** `references.bib` holds only the Lovász survey (once more under a garbled duplicate key) and Aleliunas et al. 1979. Feige and Matthews have no entries, so the writer must not invent them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4597,"cache_read_input_tokens":79421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4597,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ce9690-af02-40fd-9b57-81e661a20227","uuid":"db7e59a1-0957-4b88-bf68-2a28d7c97731","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:29:14.161Z","request_id":"req_011CgTDV3wyhw45972vwCfeQ"}
